  "grade": "artifacts:frames-continuity",
  "description": "One session's data socket across a core restart, as a run-bounded collection taps it: one tap per run. Run 1 tapped output 1 to 4, but its recording kept only 1 to 3 when the core was killed (the tap was ahead of the recording), so the new core's hello says last_committed_seq 3 and the replay starts at 4. Run 2 therefore repeats seq 4 — with the same payload and the same worker stamp, as a replay must — and the merged view takes it once: output 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, every seq once, no jump. Input is the core's own counter and is never replayed, so run 2 simply goes on at 4. A repeat inside one run, a replayed frame with other bytes or another stamp, or a jump that is not a gap frame fails.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §4.1",
    "immortality §4.2",
    "immortality §4.3",
    "decision 5.14",
    "decision 5.24"
  ],
